Patch: C linkage for SR's guest heap manager
Upstream: https://github.com/M-HT/SR at the commit pinned by SR_COMMIT in tools/pipeline.py (games/Albion/SR-Main/Game_memory.h), as staged by tools/sr_heap.py.
Original: the heap manager's C++ declarations have C++ linkage.
Replacement: wraps the declarations in extern "C".
Effect: no behavior change; the allocator functions can be called by name from the Rust runtime and from C tests.
Why: the Rust runtime links against SR's allocator and cannot call C++-mangled names.
Evidence: tools/sr_heap.py records the upstream and staged file hashes; tests/heap_lifetime.c.

--- a/Game_memory.h
+++ b/Game_memory.h
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 
+extern "C" {
+
 int x86_init_malloc(void);
 void x86_deinit_malloc(void);
 
@@ -44,6 +46,8 @@
 
 #endif
 
+} // extern "C"
+
 #else
 
 #include <stdlib.h>
